@startuml UC-004-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-004 Evaluate responses: analysis sequence diagram

control "Evaluate Response" as Eval
entity "Test Case" as TC
entity "Rubric" as R
entity "Judge Request" as JR
boundary "Judge Model Interface" as JMI
actor "Judge model" as JM
entity "Judge Evaluation" as JE

note over Eval
  Starts inside a run (UC-006), once the
  target has answered a case (UC-003).
end note

[-> Eval : evaluate(test case, actual answer)
Eval -> TC : get question, expected answer
Eval -> R : get instructions
Eval -> JR : build(instructions + output format,\nquestion, expected, actual in tags)
Eval -> JMI : send(judge request)
JMI -> JM : judge request
alt main success scenario
  JM --> JMI : verdict, justification
  JMI --> Eval : reply
  Eval -> Eval : validate reply\n(verdict is PASS or FAIL,\njustification not empty)
  Eval -> JE : create(verdict, justification,\nrubric id, judge identity)
  [<-- Eval : judge evaluation
else 2a: judge unreachable, key rejected, out of credit
  JMI --> Eval : failure
  [<-- Eval : ERROR (stage judge, reason)
else 3a: judge refuses, or its reply is cut off
  JMI --> Eval : refusal or cut-off reply
  [<-- Eval : ERROR (stage judge, reason)
else 4a: reply unreadable, no verdict, no justification
  JMI --> Eval : reply
  Eval -> Eval : validate reply fails
  [<-- Eval : ERROR (stage judge, reason)
end

note right of JE
  Business rule: a judgement that cannot be
  trusted is an ERROR, never a FAIL (AC-004-03).
end note
@enduml
